meta {
  name: UpdatePercentArtnrQueryParam
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/artikel?artnr=ZTEST-CRUD%25002
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "gewicht": 4.4
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.artnr: eq ZTEST-CRUD%002
  res.body.gewicht: eq 4.4
}

docs {
  Regression test for the double percent-decode bug: unlike
  UpdateQueryParam.bru (which uses a plain artnr with no "%"), this hits
  the ?artnr=... fallback with the artnr's literal "%" encoded using
  standard single percent-encoding (a literal "%" becomes "%25" - so
  "ZTEST-CRUD%002" is sent as "?artnr=ZTEST-CRUD%25002"). Before the
  Luna.Web.Util.QueryParamHelper fix, poRequest:URI:GetQueryValue()
  percent-decoded this twice (framework decode when building the query
  string turns "%25002" into "%002", then GetQueryValue() decodes again
  and turns the leftover "%00" into a NUL byte) - this request would come
  back 404 (artnr not found) instead of 200. Requires CreatePercentArtnr.bru
  to have run first.
}
